5":{"n":"Marina Bar","p":[["3/34/King_Nikola%27s_Palace.jpg","King Nikola's Palace","Damjan Damjanovic","CC BY 3.0",0.61],["2/20/Bar_-_centralni_gradski_trg.jpg","Bar - centralni gradski trg","Raymond Zoller from Bar, Montenegro","CC BY-SA 2.0",0.73],["2/25/Pa%C5%82ac_kr%C3%B3la_Miko%C5%82aja_w_Barze.JPG","Pałac króla Mikołaja w Barze","Marcin Konsek","CC BY-SA 4.0",0.67],["c/c0/Promenada_w_Barze.JPG","Promenada w Barze","Marcin Konsek","CC BY-SA 4.0",0.72],["3/30/Mar%C5%A1ala_Tita%2C_Bar%2C_Montenegro_-_panoramio.jpg","Maršala Tita, Bar, Montenegro","ines lukic","CC BY 3.0",0.75],["8/80/Susanj_-_panoramio.jpg","Susanj","Boro Novakovic","CC BY 3.0",0.67]],"a":["Archdiocese of Bar","The Archdiocese of Bar is a Latin Church diocese of the Catholic Church in Montenegro. It is centred in the city of Bar."]},"3318":{"n":"Marina Frapa Dubrovnik","p":[["5/50/Armoured_vehicle_Dubrovnik_Harbour.jpg","Armoured vehicle Dubrovnik Harbour","Tony Hisgett from Birmingham, UK","CC BY 2.0",0.78],["b/b7/Panorama_Dubrovnika_5059.JPG","Panorama Dubrovnika 5059","Quahadi Añtó","CC BY 3.0",0.75],["1/15/Pravoslavno_groblje%2C_Boninovo_4982.JPG","Pravoslavno groblje, Boninovo 4982","Quahadi Añtó","CC BY 3.0",1.33],["a/a7/First_boat_in_the_Croatian_Navy_%284059068128%29.jpg","First boat in the Croatian Navy","Tony Hisgett from Birmingham, UK","CC BY 2.0",0.86],["e/e4/Dubrovnik_-_panoramio_%2863%29.jpg","Dubrovnik","Frane Lovošević","CC BY-SA 3.0",0.56],["b/ba/Montenegro_Urlaub_2014_-_panoramio_%281%29.jpg","Montenegro Urlaub 2014","Jola Sik","CC BY 3.0",0.67]],"a":["Dubrovnik-Neretva County","The Dubrovnik-Neretva County is the southernmost county of Croatia. The county seat is Dubrovnik and other large towns are Korčula, Metković, Opuzen and Ploče. The Municipality of Neum, which belongs to neighbouring Bosnia and Herzegovina, divides the county in two parts which are connected only by the Pelješac Bridge. The southern part of the county consists of Dubrovnik and the surrounding area, including the Pelješac peninsula, and the islands of Korčula, Lastovo, Mljet, Šipan, Lopud and Koločep. The northern part of the county includes the Neretva Delta, the Baćina lakes north of Ploče, and a swath of hinterland near the southernmost slopes of Biokovo and around the hill of Rujnica. The northern part of the Mljet island is a national park. The Lastovo archipelago is a designated nature park. The southernmost tip of the county is the Prevlaka peninsula at the border with Montenegro. It is the only Croatian county that borders Montenegro."]},"3330":{"n":"YC Orsan","p":[["4/4f/Most_dr._Franje_Tu%C4%91mana_%2C_Dubrovnik%2C120103.JPG","Most dr. Franje Tuđmana , Dubrovnik,120103","Quahadi Añtó","CC BY 3.0",0.75],["b/b2/Most_dr._Franje_Tu%C4%91mana_%2C_Dubrovnik%2Cplo%C4%8Da120109.JPG","Most dr. Franje Tuđmana , Dubrovnik,ploča120109","Quahadi Añtó","CC BY 3.0",0.75],["8/8e/MSC_Musica_in_Dubrovnik%2C_2008.JPG","MSC Musica in Dubrovnik, 2008","Bahnfrend","CC BY-SA 3.0",0.66],["3/33/Costa_Fortuna_near_Gru%C5%BE.jpg","Costa Fortuna near Gruž","Hans Christian Haaland from Norway","CC BY 2.0",0.67],["5/52/Dr_Tudman_Bridge_Dubrovnik_%284059059182%29.jpg","Dr Tudman Bridge Dubrovnik","Tony Hisgett from Birmingham, UK","CC BY 2.0",0.64],["3/30/Bridge_Dubrovnik_%284069919400%29.jpg","Bridge Dubrovnik","Tony Hisgett from Birmingham, UK","CC BY 2.0",0.66]],"a":["Lozica, Croatia","Lozica is a village in Croatia. It is located on the D8 state road, west of Dubrovnik, on the west coast of Rijeka Dubrovačka. The Franjo Tuđman Bridge is located east of the village."]},"4093":{"n":"ACI Marina Dubrovnik","p":[["2/23/2.2.17_Dubrovnik_4_Expedition_to_Bosanka_and_Fort_Imperial_065_%2831946087871%29.jpg","2.2.17 Dubrovnik 4 Expedition to Bosanka and Fort Imperial…","donald judge","CC BY 2.0",0.67],["c/c6/31.12.16_Dubrovnik_3_Around_Sunset_56_%2831861424682%29.jpg","31.12.16 Dubrovnik 3 Around Sunset 56","donald judge","CC BY 2.0",1.5]],"a":["Lazzarettos of Dubrovnik","The Lazzarettos of 